Description: Fix SwiftShader LLVM-16 ModuleSummaryIndex C++23/libc++ compatibility
 In C++23 with libc++, std::unique_ptr requires complete types for destructors.
 GlobalValueSummary is forward-declared when used in std::vector<std::unique_ptr<GlobalValueSummary>>.
 This patch:
 - Replaces std::unique_ptr<GlobalValueSummary> with raw pointers
 - Adds explicit destructor after GlobalValueSummary is fully defined
 - Updates all call sites to use .release() instead of std::move()
Author: Juan Manuel Mendez <vejeta@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2025-11-22

